<<<
close C. the door, the window, your

mouth, used in the literal sense &

in everyday speech instead of shut,

expose the speaker to grave sus-

picion of GENTEELISM, though The

door is closed for ever upon that possi-

bility, & similar figurative uses, are innocent. See also FORMAL WORDS.
===
**close** *C. the door, the window, your mouth,* used in the literal sense & in everyday speech instead of *shut,* expose the speaker to grave suspicion of ^^GENTEELISM^^, though *The door is closed for ever upon that possibility,* & similar figurative uses, are innocent. See also ^^FORMAL WORDS^^.
>>>

